WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.198
This is the False God's Hymn.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:12.389
A soundtrack for the Amygdala that's left over in the files of Bloodborne's Network Test,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.289
And this hymn eventually became the track known as Hail the Nightmare, which is played as you explore

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:22.768
Yahar'gul, an area that's littered with Amygdala.

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:30.089
I'm playing that song for you in the background here, but I kind of prefer the original. Don't you?

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.540
The community has discovered so much hidden content in these games over the past year or so,

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.449
And it's all thanks to this small

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:46.139
But really dedicated community of hackers and data diggers who will all be listed in the description.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:52.229
So let's start with something that for me made me want to make this video in the first place.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:01:00.210
It's the recovery of every single epitaph description hidden within the network test files of Dark Souls 3.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.440
So in case you've forgotten,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.400
Epitaphs were those little gravestones that you could read in the network test,

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:11.240
And back then there was only four of them, but it turns out

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:18.460
43 of them were actually in the game's files at the time, and now every single unused epitaph has been

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.640
Extracted and then translated and then re-added to the game for our enjoyment.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:31.460
That said though, most of these only add context to characters and not much more, the context is important

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:38.729
It gives flavor to the environment and the characters. One of my favorites is this epitaph which talks about the

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:41.609
Dedication of the Abyss Watchers. It reads,

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:47.549
"Grave of a brave army. A man who fights the abyss, will die with a dull blade."

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:54.240
There's also this really sad one which is about the half-dragon creatures in Irithyll dungeon

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:59.540
Whose misery was actually entertainment for the lords of Anor Londo. It reads,

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:06.859
"It was neither a human, nor a dragon. In sadness, he danced to the royal family. Here, he sleeps."

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:13.999
There's even a line about the dedication of the Lothric Knights, which reads, "Fear the night.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.869
Loyalty beyond death to the undying King," which is cool because it's an example of a hollow Knight

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.720
Still being dedicated to the King even though they're hollowed.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:33.340
And finally, we have this odd epitaph which says, "Viewers who clicketh the bell next to the subscribe button will be notified of

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:34.530
new videos."

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.000
Such good lore.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.240
But perhaps the most interesting ones are those talking about the Pilgrims.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:46.969
These descriptions make a ton of mentions of Heaven and Hell, and they emphasize how the Pilgrims have

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.999
This longing to climb the high wall, and

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:57.200
They're scattered all throughout the game and they really drive home just how difficult the Pilgrims journeys have been.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:02.900
And considering the only Pilgrims to turn into angels are actually those who make it to World's End,

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.520
Maybe turning into an angel is their reward for making it to the end of the world.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:14.300
For all of those epitaphs and more you can check out Lance's channel where he's dictated all

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:21.889
43 of them, but of all the things changed in Dark Souls 3's development epitaphs might actually be the most minor

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.799
Because here's something big. What you're seeing now is what remains of Dark Souls 3's

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:34.339
Scrapped bonfire creation mechanic. These animations were extracted by ZullieTheWitch and

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.760
Exposed by Sanadsk. Links in the description.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.770
And can you imagine what it would have been like if it was possible for you to drag

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:48.079
Corpses to a location of your choosing and then create a bonfire wherever you like?

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:53.560
It's rumored that this is what you can see this character doing in the opening cutscene.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:59.040
At its best, this mechanic would have made the world feel like a really grand adventure,

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.680
Because imagine if you were sort of pushing through a really difficult level.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:09.240
You know you're risking death and you want to get as far as you possibly can before creating a next checkpoint, right?

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.280
So you finally decide, "Yep. This is as far as I can go."

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.840
So you create a bonfire and you sort of make a camp in that sense.

00:04:17.979 --> 00:04:23.579
You rest up and then you push forward into unknown territory. I think that's a really cool feeling.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:29.039
But in reality, I feel like this system would probably feel more like

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.250
Searching through an entire parking lot

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:37.960
Wondering where the hell you parked your bonfire. "Which level was it again? Was is a yellow level?

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.520
Oh, no, I think it was an orange level!" More questions arise from this though.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.040
Could bonfires be created anywhere?

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:51.060
What if I want to put one outside a boss's fog gate? Where do we find bonfire creation tools?

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.229
And how many bonfires could I create? And honestly,

00:04:55.229 --> 00:04:59.788
It would have been a nightmare for them to balance I think, and I can see why it was scrapped.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:04.229
Anyway, once you decided where you wanted your bonfire you could do this.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.669
Back then, this was likely called a Moonlight Ceremony,

00:05:08.669 --> 00:05:15.659
And it would have changed the way that PvP works in Dark Souls 3. Thanks to leftover files in Dark Souls 3's Network Test,

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:22.289
Lance managed to hack back in the item that was required to initiate a Moonlight Ceremony.

00:05:22.449 --> 00:05:27.419
This was called a Ceremony Sword of Darkness, and it reads, "When used,

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:30.930
Perform a ceremony to envelop the world in darkness."

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:38.370
I think we sort of saw the echoes of these ceremonial swords in Anri's corpse and as a part of

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.240
Anri's questline.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:42.510
But this Ceremonial Sword instead

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:49.589
Envelops your world in darkness and the world becomes moonlit with thick fog rolling all around you.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:55.739
The lighting work here is gorgeous. You can really see the moonlight reflecting off the pavement and

00:05:56.740 --> 00:06:01.169
Slowly, but surely we are piecing together the earliest versions of this game.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:08.220
But what was the point of this moonlight state? Well, thanks to the presence of another item in the game's code

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.120
We can actually puzzle that out.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:17.459
This one is called the Ceremony Sword of Flame. "When used, invade a world that has been enveloped in darkness.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.629
Select this item to perform an invasion ceremony."

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:30.030
So therefore, instead of invasion being linked to your character's Embered state, it was actually once linked to your world state instead,

00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:34.979
Making your world the arena to invade, not your character.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:42.160
But there was one more ceremony sword and it was called Ceremony Sword Battle Royale Eclipse,

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.000
And before you freak out, don't worry:

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.819
They probably never intended to turn Dark Souls into Fortnite,

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:51.929
Even though I actually think a battle royale mode would work pretty well for Dark Souls.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:07:00.690
No. In the past Battle Royale was simply a term that From Software used to describe their arena PvP modes, and

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:08.680
Perhaps this item would have invaded a bunch of friendly phantoms and enemy phantoms to sort of dish it out in your world.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:14.880
But in the end the only world state we got was the Eclipse State. We could have had so many more,

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.600
Some of which are absolutely breathtaking.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:26.520
This one is called Evening or Dusk, and it paints the world in these really nice sort of Twilight hues.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:32.579
This one is called Moonlit Night, and it casts some serious shadows on the environment

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:38.309
With a moon sort of silhouetting your surroundings in a wonderfully cinematic way

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:43.929
Here in Irithyll, we see the moon which isn't too different to that of the final game.

00:07:44.509 --> 00:07:48.189
But of course the world wasn't always devoid of light in these states

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:55.840
Because one of the most striking world states was this one with an enormous burning Sun overhead.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.709
I kind of understand Solaire's obsession all of a sudden.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:08.380
Then we have the Eclipse State which was a sort of blue variant with a ring of light around it. And finally we have an

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:12.880
Incredibly surreal scene that I never thought I would see in-game

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:15.229
So these

00:08:15.229 --> 00:08:21.519
Dragon creatures were featured in one of the earliest leaked screenshots of Dark Souls 3, and

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:27.969
While this scene clearly inspired the scene that we got in the full game with the Pilgrim butterflies,

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:33.040
These worm dragon like creatures are pretty different.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:40.400
They even cast shadows upon the ground which gives you a real sense that they're actually up there, above you.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:45.560
Imagine if Dark Souls had a scene like this in game where the Dragons returns to the world.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:50.709
This is the sort of thing that makes me hope that they'll get to Dark Souls 4 one day

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:54.339
Because it's clear that they have so many unused ideas

00:08:54.339 --> 00:09:01.419
just waiting in the wings. Many of these ideas actually had to do with the concept of the past and

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:09.159
time travel. There actually is a time of day filter called the Past in Dark Souls 3, which gives a sort of

00:09:09.709 --> 00:09:16.629
Grayscale look to the environment, and it's very very similar to what you would have experienced in Dark Souls 2's memory trips.

00:09:17.209 --> 00:09:19.209
Lance, who discovered all this,

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:25.480
Points out that every area that's currently accessible does have a past filter applied to it,

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:29.240
And imagine how good it would be for the story of the game if we could sort of

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:33.580
See what the world was like in the past and see what changed in the future.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:41.070
Speaking of the past the Dark Souls 2's original story actually used to be based around the concept of time travel and

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:45.059
No Soulsborne game has more cut content than Dark Souls 2.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:51.089
So this was stated in the design works, but Dark Souls 2 actually had a really really troubled development.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:57.640
About halfway through From Software thought that it was best to overhaul the entire game,

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:04.200
Which left behind a lot of old assets that originally had very different purposes. Luckily,

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.960
Echoes of the old game still remain in the files, and

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:15.749
Thanks to the work of Sanadsk and Lokey to translate, we get a rare glimpse into what the previous plot of Dark Souls 2

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:23.190
was going to be. Put simply, time travel was at the core of the story, and what you're seeing on screen now is a

00:10:23.529 --> 00:10:28.469
Recreation of a very important scholar character named Vel Derek (?) who

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:33.539
Was obsessed with a powerful artifact called The Pendulum of Time.

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:38.699
Those amongst you with great memories will remember that this blue

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:44.520
Frozen globe was actually involved in some of the earliest marketing materials for the game,

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:49.919
But nothing about its design actually ended up making it through to the final game.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:56.400
That is except for the dialogue of the scholar which was hidden deep within the game's files.

00:10:56.709 --> 00:11:01.169
Vel Derek (?) says that to activate the Pendulum, we would have had to find two things.

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:09.000
First, we have to find the Dragon's Jewel, which was a rare gem that dwells within the womb of an ancient dragon,

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:12.760
Which is probably related to the ancient dragon we fight in the Dragon Shrine.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:18.920
And second, to get the Pendulum to work, we needed to find the Drop of Time, and this one's really interesting.

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:26.850
So the Drop of Time was rumored to have been discovered by a miner who dug deep below a village that

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:36.360
Ended up being destroyed by demons. And apparently when he dug below the water there opened up a hole in space and time,

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:40.520
Teleporting the miner to a different location far above ground.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.640
Does that remind you of anything?

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:50.760
Honestly, this sounds borderline identical to the ruined city cutscene that's seen in the opening, especially since there's water,

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.480
There's a giant hole in the ground,

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:55.880
It teleports us to a place above ground in a different time, and

00:11:56.339 --> 00:12:01.159
You even see the city untouched by time in the reflection of the water.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:07.129
So once you put the Pendulum of Time together with the Drop of Time and the Dragon Gem,

00:12:07.499 --> 00:12:13.639
This presumably would have led us to another character who is discovered within Dark Souls 2's files,

00:12:14.189 --> 00:12:21.139
The child version of the Emerald Herald. This might be the cutest character to ever grace the Souls series.

00:12:21.509 --> 00:12:27.079
The Emerald Herald, in case you've forgotten, was half-dragon and she was half-human, and

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:32.899
She gives you the aged feather which apparently was an item from her childhood

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:38.160
That she looked at and with it she conjured up a world of endless possibilities.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:42.640
The way that she gives our character this item in the opening cutscene is

00:12:43.319 --> 00:12:45.319
Honestly kind of heart-wrenching,

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:51.649
Almost as if she's imploring us to sort of remember her, as if they completely filled out her story,

00:12:51.689 --> 00:12:56.269
We actually would have gone back in time and have known her when she was still a child.

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:59.809
You can check out Senadsk's video on the topic for more.

00:13:00.269 --> 00:13:04.519
In recent years even Bloodborne has been dug into which is a

00:13:04.709 --> 00:13:11.568
Notoriously difficult task as there's no PC version for the game. Nevertheless, the community always finds a way.

00:13:11.759 --> 00:13:14.329
This is an unseen animation from Bloodborne.

00:13:14.329 --> 00:13:17.959
It was once used to crush a liver above your character,

00:13:18.209 --> 00:13:22.758
For before there was cold blood there were fresh livers. There were large fresh livers,

00:13:22.759 --> 00:13:28.639
There were very large fresh livers and so on, which could be crushed to give you some blood echoes on demand.

00:13:29.369 --> 00:13:34.849
In our bodies, the liver can actually hold up to like 10% of the body's blood at any given time,

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:40.189
So it actually makes some sense for this item to be a realistic source of blood echoes

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:46.350
Although at the time the resource given was still called souls, and just like souls,

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:49.679
You could actually get the fresh livers of bosses as well

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:55.049
Which reveals the names of the original bosses that were planned to be in Bloodborne.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:58.109
Some of the most interesting ones up on the screen.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:04.380
Bloodborne even had a character editor at one point which was a way to reverse any horrible

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:11.460
Abominations that you regretted making at the start of the game. All you had to do was step up to this mirror

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:18.179
I bet most people haven't even noticed in the hunters dream and then just wear clothing to change appearance.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:24.030
This never made it into the game, and I'm not really sure why because out of all the games

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:29.099
Being able to change your appearance in a dream actually make some sense.

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:33.179
But unlike the mirror I can see why they removed these.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:40.500
These were called Warp Chairs and there was something for your character to sit in, fall asleep in and then

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:46.949
Drift off to the Hunter's Dream in. There was an assortment of chair designs, but no matter what they look like,

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:53.609
There's a problem with these because in some environments they barely even look out of place. So

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:57.749
Imagine being about to die in Bloodborne. You're out of blood vials,

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:02.190
You're desperately going up to random chairs and just hoping that it's a checkpoint.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.219
Yeah, I can see why they removed it.

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:11.700
It's also possible that they simply moved this concept over to Micolash and his students who

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.920
all drift off to their nightmare in a really similar fashion.

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:17.440
And number 10

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:23.219
Finally is a personal favorite of mine and it's something that I actually wish I could have come up with an excuse to talk about

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:26.100
At the time because put simply, a

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:31.169
Dedicated group of Chalice Dungeon prospectors recently discovered a whole new

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:36.569
Labyrinth that had never been explored before and it had some fascinating bosses inside.

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:39.000
There's a full explanation in the description,

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:43.559
But put simply, this small team of dungeon prospectors managed to

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:47.820
Identify a glitch that causes only 32 out of

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:55.670
200 possible Chalice Dungeons to appear in its chalices which means that we've been locked out of ton of

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:59.720
Dungeons until now. So to get around this, they painstakingly

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:03.890
Rolled back their saves every single time that they wanted to

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:11.330
Explore a little bit further, and they kept doing this and mapping out the dungeons until they stumbled upon something

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.840
Really special. They found wandering bosses.

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:20.270
So these bosses actually appear simply, without fog gates or a giant health bar,

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:26.299
Just wandering through the dungeon. And according to their Reddit post, 5 have been found so far.

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:31.609
There's the Abhorrent Beast, there's the Blood Starved Beast, there's the Pthumerian Descendant,

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:37.280
There's the Pthumerian Elder, and there's the Watchdog of the Old Lords. And they're just wandering around

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:45.530
Like other aggroable enemies. For me personally, Chalice Dungeons have always been one of the most tedious things in the Soulsborne series,

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:53.119
So I respect the hell out of anyone who's capable of having the patience to explore hundreds of these dungeons and

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:55.310
Map them out. That's crazy.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:17:03.439
And the fact that they managed to discover something in a three-year-old game without the use of digging into the data of the game is

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.370
Really, really impressive.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:12.680
So in conclusion, all of these people have kept content for these games going long after many of us have dropped them,

00:17:12.839 --> 00:17:19.819
So we should show them some support and check out their channels and the users below in the description because

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:22.579
There is some seriously good stuff down there.

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:28.039
Thank you all for watching and I'll see you next time and the next video is a Prepare to Cry. I promise.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:30.160
(Subs done By A Trash Can, edited by DoctorAgon)

